WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.506
Today is three letters. Each one starts with a line down.

2
00:00:03.956 --> 00:00:04.750
These three.

3
00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.929
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

4
00:00:08.429 --> 00:00:13.341
The first one. Start at the top line. Pull straight down to the bottom line. That is all.

5
00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:20.496
The next one is small. Start at the dotted line. Pull down. Then lift, and add a dot.

6
00:00:21.936 --> 00:00:26.911
The last one is tall. Start near the top. Pull down. Then lift, and go across.

7
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:34.532
On the page, your child puts a finger on the green dot, traces the big letter, and says its path out loud.

8
00:00:34.982 --> 00:00:39.368
Saying it matters. The words are what the hand remembers when you are not there.

9
00:00:39.818 --> 00:00:44.662
Then step away. Your child traces the gray letters, always from the green dot.

10
00:00:45.112 --> 00:00:50.655
For the last two rows they cover the big letters with a book, and write with no gray letters to help.

11
00:00:51.105 --> 00:00:58.037
After each row, your child circles their own best letter. Looking for the best one is how they check their own work.

12
00:00:58.487 --> 00:01:04.687
At the end, they write two letters and one word while you watch the pencil. Mark each one that starts at the top.
